      "subtopic": "breastfeeding",
      "claim": "Information on the use of risperidone during breastfeeding is limited. When taken in doses of up to 6 mg a day, risperidone was found in breast milk in small amounts. Side effects were not reported in a small number of breastfed infants. If you suspect the baby has any symptoms (being more sleepy than usual, jitteriness, poor feeding, crankiness, or unusual movements) contact the child’s healthcare provider.",
